--TEST--
A class in a loaded extension's source section resolves with no `autoload` line, compiles like the program's own code and calls the extension's class — `rule:packaging/an-extension-package-carries-two-payloads`
--EXTENSION--
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Shop\Ledger\Receipt;

// `Receipt` comes with the `ledger` extension. The program needs no `autoload` line for it.
echo Receipt::line("Tea", 250), "\n";
--EXPECT--
Tea: 250 EUR
